          "message": "feat(specs): zkSPARQL — Zero-Knowledge Query Proofs over SPARQL, Unofficial Proposal Draft (sq-rvgr2.2) (#1333)\n\n* feat(specs): zkSPARQL Unofficial Proposal Draft — zero-knowledge query proofs over SPARQL (sq-rvgr2.2)\n\nAuthors the second /specs draft from the prose estate-recon digest\n(research/specs/zksparql-estate-recon.md, docs/fable-program-recon-records):\nthe committed data model (RDFC-1.0 + Poseidon2/BN254, Baby-Jubjub Schnorr\nattestations), the bucketed SPARQL fragment + CircuitId family, the\nProofManifest interchange object + sub-proof/public-input encoding, the\nverifier-nonce challenge-response, the fail-closed verifier obligation set\n(12 bind_* + structural re-checks + the four audit gates), external trust\nanchors, the sec-prop/secx vocabulary + over-claim rule, and the ODRL\nadmissibility profile. Missing pieces (media type, JSON-LD context, wire\nprotocol, portable test vectors, normative fragment grammar) are labelled\nexplicit proposals/gaps; code-pinned details carry Editor's notes for a\nlater transcription pass rather than being invented.\n\nHONESTY: the draft states plainly — in the abstract, an audit-status box,\nthe over-claim rule, and the Security and Privacy Considerations — that the\nestate is research-grade, NOT externally audited (open gate sq-qhy4), that\nsoundness/attestation are not production-ready, and that the hidden-holder\ntiers are labelled not-yet-sound. Both honesty gates (no-perf-numbers\n--enforce, check-privacy-claims) pass; spec factory builds PDF+HTML for\nboth registered specs; all 293 site unit tests green.\n\nAuthored strictly from the prose digest; no crates/ sources were read.\n\nSPARQ-Agent: dispatched as Claude Fable 5 (optimistic-first protocol; exact model marker reconciled post-hoc by the orchestrator)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(specs): zkSPARQL draft rev 2 — threat model, normative-kernel re-scope, fragment semantics, provenance citations (sq-rvgr2.2)\n\nAddresses review round 1 on PR #1333 (all 8 must-fix + 3 overclaims):\n\n- Re-scope (must-fix 1/6): the document now declares itself an architecture\n  overview with an explicitly enumerated normative kernel (new section 2);\n  the five security-load-bearing cores still pinned only by the\n  implementation (leaf encoding, manifest schema + canonicalisation, Q6\n  guard, bind_* clauses, public-input layout) are named as deferred cores\n  blocking any candidate-normative successor (tracked as bead sq-rvgr2.7).\n  The circular \"conforming verifier MUST implement every obligation\" clause\n  is replaced by provisional conformance classes that say plainly what may\n  and may not be claimed; the manifest-canonicalisation \"not conformant\"\n  MUST is downgraded to an honest dependency statement.\n- Threat model (must-fix 2): new section 5 — parties/trust relationships,\n  adversary capabilities (malicious prover, curious verifier,\n  holder-issuer collusion, network, quantum), per-goal definitions of\n  soundness/completeness/binding/hiding/replay-resistance with\n  mechanism + honest status, and an out-of-scope list; placed before the\n  mechanism sections.\n- Semantic anchor (must-fix 3): new section 7.2 gives the fragment a\n  normative grammar + Pérez–Arenas–Gutiérrez algebra evaluation over the\n  RDF 1.1 graph model under simple entailment (cites PAG09, RDF11-MT), and\n  defines bind_query_correctness's target property (result membership),\n  with the set/bag, projection, and completeness boundaries flagged.\n- Related work + provenance (must-fix 4): new section 3 positions against\n  IntegriDB/vSQL/ZKSQL, CL/BBS selective disclosure, and prior zk-over-RDF\n  work; SEC-PROP is now properly attributed to Wright, Shadbolt, Zhao,\n  Zhao, Braun (verified against zksparql.org + CEUR-WS Vol-4085 on\n  2026-07-01) and declared as the editor's own prior work; added BN254\n  (Barreto–Naehrig), Schnorr, and Pedersen commitment references.\n- RFC-2119 misuse (must-fix 5, overclaim 3): the reverse-engineered\n  public-input byte layout (section 8.4) is now descriptive and at-risk,\n  with no normative keywords.\n- Audit gates (must-fix 7): section 10.4 now defines the four audit gates\n  in a 1:1 table (gate 3 = bind_issuer_attestations, enforced per scan)\n  and states that backend proof verification carries no gate number.\n- Worked example + schema (must-fix 8): section 8.2 member-schema table\n  (pinned vs not-transcribed rows) and section 8.5 illustrative manifest\n  with a decoded sub-proof blob showing the verifier nonce at public-input\n  field 0.\n- Overclaims corrected: \"specifies\" -> \"describes\" (abstract + intro);\n  per-obligation forge-test claims softened to the obligation SET being\n  covered by the forge suite (sections 10.3 + 16), since the grounding\n  digest records the suite collectively.\n\nGates: build-specs (no-perf-numbers honesty scan) green, full next static\nexport green, ESLint green, tsc --noEmit green, 293/293 site unit tests.\nAuthored strictly from the prose digest; no crates/ sources were read.\n\nSPARQ-Agent: dispatched as Claude Fable 5 (optimistic-first protocol; exact model marker reconciled post-hoc by the orchestrator)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(specs): replace TODO markers with bead sq-rvgr2.7 refs + trim zkSPARQL index blurb (sq-rvgr2.2) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nAddress Copilot review threads on PR #1333:\n- Remove all 7 'TODO:' placeholders from the zkSPARQL editor's notes (repo\n  hygiene forbids TODO markers in docs); each now references bead sq-rvgr2.7\n  as the transcription-tracking task instead. Meaning preserved; honesty\n  caveats untouched.\n- Trim the over-long /specs index blurb (rendered verbatim on the index card,\n  the per-spec subtitle, and the page meta description) to a single concise\n  sentence, keeping the 'research-grade and NOT externally audited (sq-qhy4)'\n  honesty caveat.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(specs): privacy-claims honesty markers on zkSPARQL .typ — pre-empt the extended gate (sq-rvgr2.2) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe privacy-claims gate now scans site/specs/**/*.typ (sq-rvgr2.5). Two lines in\nzksparql.typ are legitimate over-matches of the coarse phrase regex:\n- an explicit anti-overclaim (\"not... let alone provably sound ... verifier\")\n- a prior-work bibliography title (Wright, ISWC 2025 DC)\nEach gets an inline `privacy-claims-allow:` marker recording the honest why; no\ncapability wording weakened. `scripts/check-privacy-claims.sh` and `npm run\nbuild-specs` both exit 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
