          "message": "feat(engine): M4 Phase 2 DataChunk::decode_numeric_column decode primitive + inline-int gather-free fast path (sq-pntvh.2) [OPUS-4.8] (#1365)\n\nThe columnar `select_numeric` kernel re-gathers `numeric_value(id)` per element\n(a random-access value-cache lookup + a branch — the same access pattern the row\npath pays, not auto-vectorisable). This adds `DataChunk::decode_numeric_column`:\ngather an id column ONCE into a contiguous `Vec<f64>` value column with an\n`f64::NAN` sentinel for non-numeric cells, after which every downstream compare /\nreduce is a branchless loop the compiler auto-vectorises. An all-inline-integer\ncolumn takes a gather-free straight-line fast path (the value is in the id,\n`id - INLINE_BASE`), bit-identical to the general path.\n\nThe NaN sentinel drops straight into the existing numeric kernels: `VecCmp::test`\nalready rejects NaN under every operator, so a non-numeric cell is excluded at the\ncompare step exactly as the row FILTER's type-error path excludes it — no side\nvalidity bitmap. Direct unit tests prove decode matches the scalar per-id decode\nover a MIXED inline-int / dict-id / non-numeric column (bit-exact, incl. the NaN\nsentinel), the inline fast path is exact, and decode+VecCmp selects exactly what\n`select_numeric` keeps. The sentinel check is non-vacuous (a 0.0 sentinel fails it).\n\nAll behind the existing `vectorized` feature (OFF by default): feature-OFF is\nbyte-identical, no new deps, `forbid(unsafe_code)`-clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-02T16:59:20Z",
          "tree_id": "f1264ad3760310d156104bd510d16f080d57cda5",
          "url": "https://github.com/jeswr/sparq/commit/678fd141d12973c9566cc73955014d1cf9368740"
